d Section 3: Later Years and Legacy*  \nIn his later years Raymond III endured additional sieges including one by the Egyptian sultan Qalawun in 1265. The city fell briefly before Raymond negotiated its return. He died in 1270 leaving a fractured realm divided among his heirs. Though a crusader hero Raymond’s rule was marred by financial strain and factionalism. His legacy remains complex embodying both dedication to Christianity and the fragility of Latin Christian power in the East.', 'num_tokens': 1455, 'context_tokens': 131, 'sum_logits': -535.6387156343814, 'reasoning_content': 'Okay, so I need to write a 300+ word summary of the Raymond III, Count of Tripoli page from Wikipedia. The user specified not to use any commas and to highlight at least three sections with markdown titles like *Highlighted Section 1*, etc. Let me start by recalling what I know about Raymond III. He was a Crusader ruler, right? From the Maronite dynasty. His father was Bohemond VI, so he was a member of that family. He ruled Tripoli in the 13th century, I think around the mid-1200s.\n\nFirst, I need to check the key points from the Wikipedia page. Let me imagine the structure. The main sections would include his background, reign, conflicts, family, and legacy. Since the user wants three highlighted sections, I need to identify the most important parts. Maybe his rise to power after his father\'s death, his conflicts with the Egyptians and others, and his later life or death?\n\nWait, the user said not to use any commas. That means I have to structure sentences without them. Maybe use periods or other punctuation. Also, the highlights need to be in markdown, so I\'ll use asterisks around the section titles. Let me outline the summary first.\n\nStart with an intro about Raymond III, his title, family background. Then his early life and succession. His reign\'s key events: conflicts with Egypt, maybe the Barons\' Wars? He was involved in the conflict with the Egyptian Mamluks, right? Ther